  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>digit numbers whose sum of digits is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>, is ..........",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "54",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;be the three-digit number such that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Thus, total number of non-negative integral solution&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>11</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn></math></p><p>But for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, so required number of integers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></math>.</p>",
